    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d516">

                <pb facs="0684" n="564" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg564"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Iddings to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Rome,
                            Italy</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1905-04-05"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">April 5, 1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 478.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith
                    passport No. 2816, issued by this embassy on July 5, 1904, to one Ralph
                        Gironda.<anchor n="a" xml:id="d516-f1"/> It appears that this passport was
                    presented at the inspection for the steamship <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Canopic</hi> March 15, 1905, by an individual who was palpably not the
                    owner thereof. A copy of a letter from the consul at Naples to the
                    consul-general at Rome in regard to this matter is also sent under this
                    cover.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lewis Morris
                    Iddings.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d516-a1.xml" xpointer="d516-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
